### Scope boundaries

The notebook demonstrates local processes, not a multi-node deployment. It
replaces one stateless function module, not a whole application release. It
reconstructs a worker from initial parameters, not a durable checkpoint. It
checks numerical equivalence, not acceleration. It preserves Sher's motivation
without treating concurrency, supervision, or code loading as proof that general
intelligence or automatic self-repair follows.

**End of Chapter 5.**
